It builds on the FOSSBot open-source educational robot
(https://github.com/eellak/fossbot, MIT License):

- ws/src/fossbot_description contains a URDF and STL meshes of the FOSSBot v2,
  derived from the `fossbot_educational_description` package of the FOSSBot
  Gazebo simulation, with the gazebo plugin block removed (on real hardware the
  bridge publishes those topics instead). scripts/sync_description.sh
  re-vendors them.
- robot_agent/pinmap.py follows the FOSSBot v2 main PCB schematic.
- The encoder disc resolution (20 slots) matches the upstream FOSSBot Python
  library.
